Fix the hover flicker bug in SkillTreeLab.svelte.

## The Problem
When hovering over skill nodes, they flicker. This is because `.node-group:hover { transform: scale(1.2) }` shifts the node under the cursor, causing mouseleave -> scale back -> mouseenter -> loop.

## The Fix
Add an invisible hit-area circle to each node group that's larger than the visible node, so the cursor stays within the hit area even when the node scales up.

In the `{#each visibleNodes}` block, add a transparent circle BEFORE the glow/node circles:

```svelte
<!-- Hit area (invisible, prevents hover flicker) -->
<circle
  r={radius + 10}
  fill="transparent"
  stroke="none"
/>
```

Also change the hover transform in CSS from `transform: scale(1.2)` to use `transform-origin: center` and a smaller scale like `scale(1.15)` to keep it subtle.

Do NOT change any other logic or styling. Only fix the flicker.
